  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>oxytocin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>H01BB02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>De Groot AN et al. 1995</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>male volunteers</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>oxytocin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_oxytocin/Oxytocin_De1995_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>distribution half-life</td><td>0.049</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2α</small></td></tr><tr><td>elimination half-life</td><td>0.33</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2β</small></td></tr><tr><td>total body clearance</td><td>67.1</td><td>L h-1</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution</td><td>33.2</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>absorption half-life</td><td>0.45</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2ka </small></td></tr><tr><td>apparent elimination half-life</td><td>0.69</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr></table><h4>About oxytocin</h4><p>Oxytocin is a peptide hormone used as a uterotonic drug to induce or support labour and manage bleeding after childbirth. It is widely used in human medicine, appears on the WHO essential medicines list, and is also approved for veterinary use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q169960\">Wikidata Q169960</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Oxytocin\">Oxytocin</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>De Groot AN et al. (1995). Bioavailability and pharmacokinetics of sublingual oxytocin in male volunteers. <i>The Journal of pharmacy and pharmacology 47(7):571–575</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.2042-7158.1995.tb06716.x\">10.1111/j.2042-7158.1995.tb06716.x</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8568623\">8568623</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from De_1995: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
